WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.760
Speaker 1: [rock music]

2
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:55.440
Speaker 1: Mortal

3
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.480
Speaker 1: Steel: Episode nine.

4
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.300
Speaker 1: [footsteps] Dr. Marie Singer waited

5
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.400
Speaker 1: by the door. Paced by the door,
anyway. Was she going to come?

6
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.960
Speaker 1: Or maybe she would turn them in. What
would happen to her?

7
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.060
Speaker 1: Maybe she could convince them
Francesca and Ursula were not involved.

8
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:27.820
Speaker 1: Ursula was kneeling at the foot of
her bed, head bowed in silent prayer. Marie had

9
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:33.420
Speaker 1: kept a similar habit once. There
wasn't a better time to pray for help.

10
00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:39.880
Speaker 1: No, the Lord helped those who helped
themselves. Meanwhile,

11
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:45.900
Speaker 1: Francesca was examining a light
fixture. Oh, wait. She had it

12
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:46.660
Speaker 1: dismantled.

13
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.960
Speaker 2: Francesca, stop it. Put that back.

14
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.520
Speaker 1: The woman ripped something electronic
free from the lighting fixture.

15
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.000
Speaker 3: It was bugged. Video and audio by the
looks of it.

16
00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.540
Speaker 2: And now they know you know. Did you
think about that?

17
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.360
Speaker 1: Francesca looked down at the thing in
her hand, dumbfounded.

18
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:13.500
Speaker 3: Oh. I could put it back.

19
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.220
Speaker 2: Just... [sighs]

20
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:23.100
Speaker 1: She reached toward her face with
claw-like hands gripping the air.

21
00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:27.660
Speaker 2: Don't touch anything else. Okay?

22
00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.620
Speaker 3: Yeah, okay. Chill out.

23
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:37.040
Speaker 1: Blessedly, their dorm room door slid
open and Kelly Jon Fore slipped

24
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:42.540
Speaker 1: cautiously into the room with eyes
wide. She was dressed in all black.

25
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.000
Speaker 2: Why are you wearing that?

26
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.020
Speaker 3: I was sneaking.

27
00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.000
Speaker 1: Marie pressed her palms to her face
and let out a silent scream.

28
00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.260
Speaker 1: Francesca held out the severed camera
toward Kelly.

29
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.540
Speaker 2: Who's watching us?

30
00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.320
Speaker 4: I am.

31
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:09.680
Speaker 1: Kelly Jon Fore visibly withered,
gasping like a fish out of water.

32
00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.740
Speaker 1: This was a little more direct than
she'd hoped for, but trying to keep any of these

33
00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:21.560
Speaker 1: people covert was clearly a lost
cause. Still, she felt bad for

34
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.060
Speaker 1: dragging the young mother into this.
Hopefully, they had not angered this creature.

35
00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.040
Speaker 2: Are you the intercom?

36
00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.120
Speaker 4: Yes, and before you ask, no, you're
not prisoners here. You may leave at any time

37
00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.100
Speaker 4: through the way you entered.

38
00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.600
Speaker 3: Yeah, right.

39
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.180
Speaker 1: If they were going for antagonistic,
Marie may as well try to get some information

40
00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:45.620
Speaker 1: out of it.

41
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.200
Speaker 2: Why are you stealing children?

42
00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.120
Speaker 4: I have never stolen a child. They
were donated.

43
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.320
Speaker 1: [gasps] Kelly Jon Fore snapped out of
her stupor.

44
00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.180
Speaker 3: Liar. You took him.

45
00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:05.600
Speaker 4: You knew the price of admission. As
did your parents, and their parents before them.

46
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.140
Speaker 4: Survival comes at a cost. If you do
not wish to pay it, you may leave.

47
00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.340
Speaker 1: Kelly screamed at the intercom.

48
00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.700
Speaker 3: [screams]

49
00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:20.500
Speaker 1: Slamming her fist into the speaker
until it bled. It was a blind, mindless rage.

50
00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:25.780
Speaker 1: Marie tried to gently pull her away,
but the woman spun on her, something feral in

51
00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:31.660
Speaker 1: her eyes. She stood tense, ready to
fight, ready to kill, but the

52
00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:37.300
Speaker 1: speaker could not be killed. The rage
bled out of Kelly and she sunk to the floor,

53
00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:38.720
Speaker 1: sobbing.

54
00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.080
Speaker 3: [cries] What did you do to him?

55
00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.400
Speaker 3: What did you do to my baby?

56
00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:57.200
Speaker 1: Marie couldn't take it anymore, the
fire in her chest, the rage stoked by this

57
00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:01.860
Speaker 1: woman's suffering. It demanded
violence, and it demanded it now.

58
00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:03.420
Speaker 2: Get up.

59
00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.680
Speaker 1: Kelly looked up at her with
tear-filled eyes.

60
00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.540
Speaker 2: Get your husband and your baby. We're
leaving.

61
00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.960
Speaker 1: Marie glanced at the other sisters,
but they were clearly coming with her. Not even

62
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:24.580
Speaker 1: Francesca offered a word of rebuke.
They rose and left the room and paced down the

63
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.860
Speaker 1: hall at a speed just below blind
panic. Marie could feel the eyes of cameras on
her,

64
00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:35.500
Speaker 1: could feel whatever time they had to
escape ticking down like the grains of an

65
00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:41.140
Speaker 1: hourglass. When it ran out, there
would be no escape. The

66
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:46.460
Speaker 1: intercom, whatever it was, it would
not tolerate traitors for long.

67
00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:52.440
Speaker 1: It created a horrible pressure, like
standing in the jaws of a closing mouth.

68
00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:57.680
Speaker 1: Kelly Jon Fore ran fingers through
her hair, muttering to herself.

69
00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.220
Speaker 3: What am I doing?

70
00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:05.780
Speaker 2: You're making the right choice. We
can protect you out there

71
00:06:07.248 --> 00:06:12.788
Speaker 1: blatant falsehood. Mostly. When
they'd fled Last Respite, they'd been certain
they

72
00:06:12.828 --> 00:06:18.808
Speaker 1: could not return for fear of
political fallout. Now Marie would gladly
welcome

73
00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:23.868
Speaker 1: a prison cell if one was on offer.
Anything was better than this place.

74
00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:30.828
Speaker 1: And the moment they were safe, she
was going to make a call. Cyborg number

75
00:06:31.048 --> 00:06:34.268
Speaker 1: four was gonna tear this place apart.

76
00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:38.848
Speaker 1: That was when the lights went out.

77
00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:46.068
Speaker 1: [dramatic music]

78
00:06:46.148 --> 00:06:46.228
Speaker 3: [gasps]

79
00:06:46.288 --> 00:06:49.108
Speaker 4: Important to stay in your rooms due
to the toxic gas.

80
00:06:50.288 --> 00:06:51.368
Speaker 1: Oh, hell.

81
00:06:53.808 --> 00:06:59.068
Speaker 1: It wasn't the soft whisping of gas
she heard in the darkness as the other people

82
00:06:59.188 --> 00:07:04.408
Speaker 1: reached out for her, grasping for
comfort and safety she could not provide.

83
00:07:05.688 --> 00:07:11.527
Speaker 1: It was the sound of servos, metal
feet clacking

84
00:07:11.607 --> 00:07:13.348
Speaker 1: on concrete floor.

85
00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:19.968
Speaker 4: I can't afford to waste resources.
Please accompany Jelly John 3. I don't think his

86
00:07:19.988 --> 00:07:23.388
Speaker 4: motor control is sufficient to
guarantee your safety if he must use force.

87
00:07:24.728 --> 00:07:29.728
Speaker 1: Dim red emergency lights lit up a
path along the floor down the hallway.

88
00:07:31.068 --> 00:07:36.348
Speaker 1: A humanoid figure covered in rags
waited for them where the trail of lights
stopped.

89
00:07:37.288 --> 00:07:41.668
Speaker 1: It stepped toward them in slow, jerky
movements.

90
00:07:43.268 --> 00:07:44.688
Speaker 3: Excuse me.

91
00:07:44.888 --> 00:07:50.308
Speaker 3: [gasps]

92
00:07:50.388 --> 00:07:53.568
Speaker 1: Part 11. Sins of Knowledge.

93
00:07:59.548 --> 00:08:05.268
Speaker 1: Ethan climbed up the incline to meet
the bikers. He tried to ignore the

94
00:08:05.348 --> 00:08:10.688
Speaker 1: pulsing veins running through the
earth and the small squid-like creature swimming

95
00:08:10.728 --> 00:08:15.748
Speaker 1: through them, following him. The lead
scary boy,

96
00:08:16.347 --> 00:08:22.008
Speaker 1: Miranda, wrinkled the half of her
face Ethan could still see and pinched her

97
00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:22.648
Speaker 1: nose.

98
00:08:24.088 --> 00:08:25.708
Speaker 3: Ugh, you smell like sewer.

99
00:08:27.808 --> 00:08:33.528
Speaker 1: Sewers haven't been cleaned in a long
time. Ethan pointed a finger gun at

100
00:08:33.568 --> 00:08:39.548
Speaker 1: Miranda and winked. You're just
trying to get out of a hug. She recoiled from

101
00:08:39.628 --> 00:08:45.128
Speaker 1: him. She was more alarmed than when
he'd threatened to turn their bodies into gifts.

102
00:08:46.668 --> 00:08:48.208
Speaker 1: What kind of world was this?

103
00:08:48.908 --> 00:08:49.848
Speaker 3: Ugh, you wouldn't.

104
00:08:50.688 --> 00:08:56.568
Speaker 1: Ethan sat back on the motorcycle. The
name Eddie was carved below the

105
00:08:56.608 --> 00:09:01.828
Speaker 1: handlebars. No, I wouldn't hug you.
But if I did,

106
00:09:03.408 --> 00:09:08.848
Speaker 1: it would be lethal. Whoa. There was
that

107
00:09:08.928 --> 00:09:14.908
Speaker 1: admiration again, after he'd
threatened to hug them to death. His second

108
00:09:14.948 --> 00:09:20.848
Speaker 1: mind was loving this heroic dialogue,
but it served no purpose. There was

109
00:09:20.908 --> 00:09:26.508
Speaker 1: a boy out there who needed saving,
and if the Stalker told any truths, the nuns

110
00:09:26.568 --> 00:09:32.388
Speaker 1: might not be running into the arms of
safety at New Hope. No more words.

111
00:09:33.048 --> 00:09:38.068
Speaker 1: Time to use a little ammunition. Now
how do we find New Hope?

112
00:09:38.908 --> 00:09:41.608
Speaker 1: Miranda nodded towards something on
the horizon.

113
00:09:42.768 --> 00:09:44.208
Speaker 3: You gotta get past those.

114
00:09:45.548 --> 00:09:50.788
Speaker 1: Ethan zoomed in on the skyline where
she watched. Helicopter drones buzzed about

115
00:09:50.848 --> 00:09:56.128
Speaker 1: over the rooftops by the dozen. His
eyes stretched to zoom even further.

116
00:09:56.948 --> 00:09:58.628
Speaker 1: They had machine guns on them.

117
00:10:00.128 --> 00:10:03.728
Speaker 3: Your eye is stretching out of your
head.

118
00:10:05.628 --> 00:10:06.828
Speaker 3: It's creepy.

119
00:10:08.288 --> 00:10:13.888
Speaker 1: Ethan swung his head and his
telescoping eye toward Miranda. Heh,

120
00:10:14.308 --> 00:10:19.808
Speaker 1: you're one to talk. The bone shield
could only hide half of her smile.

121
00:10:21.048 --> 00:10:26.748
Speaker 1: That flicker of a smile held some
hope for peace. All right, let's

122
00:10:26.828 --> 00:10:27.088
Speaker 1: go.

123
00:10:28.948 --> 00:10:29.788
Speaker 3: What's the plan?

124
00:10:31.068 --> 00:10:35.308
Speaker 1: Win. [motorcycle revs]

125
00:10:35.368 --> 00:10:36.108
Speaker 3: Works for me.

126
00:10:36.128 --> 00:11:10.128
Speaker 3: [motorcycle revs]

127
00:11:10.148 --> 00:11:10.528
Speaker 3: [crow caws] [motorcycle revs]

128
00:11:10.548 --> 00:11:14.728
Speaker 1: Ethan took a hard left to stay with
the riders. The drone swarm behind them was a

129
00:11:14.828 --> 00:11:19.748
Speaker 1: humming, flying cloud of black death.
There were more than just the gunner drones.

130
00:11:20.328 --> 00:11:24.688
Speaker 1: There were also the smaller, faster
drones with adhesive on their undersides and no

131
00:11:24.748 --> 00:11:29.168
Speaker 1: gun. It hadn't been clear what they
were for until three of them stuck to the back

132
00:11:29.208 --> 00:11:34.908
Speaker 1: of a scary boy and detonated. The
resulting pink mist painted a dangerous

133
00:11:34.968 --> 00:11:37.428
Speaker 1: picture for anyone who fell behind.

134
00:11:39.028 --> 00:11:42.988
Speaker 1: At least the gunner drones were not
of sufficient caliber to do more than ruin his

135
00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:48.128
Speaker 1: outfit. A squadron of drones appeared
at the end of the street. Bright yellow muzzle

136
00:11:48.188 --> 00:11:53.268
Speaker 1: flashes and a pattering popping
sound. One of the scary boys was torn to shreds
and

137
00:11:53.328 --> 00:11:57.148
Speaker 1: flipped over his careening motorcycle
and smashed into a ruined car.

138
00:11:57.508 --> 00:12:03.368
Speaker 1: [screams] Ethan lowered his shotgun
arm and fired. [shotgun fires] But at

139
00:12:03.428 --> 00:12:07.788
Speaker 1: this distance, the pellets did little
more than knock the drones around. The things

140
00:12:07.808 --> 00:12:12.584
Speaker 1: were so light and small that only a
perfect shot would actually shatter them. This

141
00:12:12.644 --> 00:12:18.264
Speaker 1: is no good. They could neither outrun
nor outmaneuver the gunners. If those sticky

142
00:12:18.344 --> 00:12:24.324
Speaker 1: explosive ones caught them, well,
even Ethan would feel those. He pulled up

143
00:12:24.384 --> 00:12:28.344
Speaker 1: alongside Miranda as they drove under
the gunner's squadron and took a hard right.

144
00:12:29.044 --> 00:12:32.844
Speaker 1: The drone zipped around to follow
them, peppering with more small arms fire.

145
00:12:32.844 --> 00:12:35.004
Speaker 1: [drone firing] Where do we go?

146
00:12:36.404 --> 00:12:39.024
Speaker 3: We're circling back. Your new buddy
should be set up.

147
00:12:39.704 --> 00:12:43.244
Speaker 1: He wanted to ask what she meant, but
they were forced to separate to dodge obstacles

148
00:12:43.304 --> 00:12:47.924
Speaker 1: in the road. [tires screeching] This
was the second time Ethan had been harassed by

149
00:12:48.004 --> 00:12:53.404
Speaker 1: flying opponents. It was growing
tiresome. It made a straightforward

150
00:12:53.484 --> 00:12:57.104
Speaker 1: slugfest with an opponent like the
spine eater almost appealing in retrospect.

151
00:12:58.604 --> 00:13:04.084
Speaker 1: Almost. [gun firing] Their small
mounted machine guns pointed directly at
Miranda.

152
00:13:04.504 --> 00:13:08.604
Speaker 1: She tried to angle her body so that
the bone side would block some of the fire. But

153
00:13:08.664 --> 00:13:14.464
Speaker 1: this, this is the end for her.
Unless, unless

154
00:13:14.564 --> 00:13:19.884
Speaker 1: Ethan did something stupid. He looked
down at the handlebars. No time to reload the

155
00:13:19.924 --> 00:13:25.324
Speaker 1: shotgun. Then he released the
handlebars and stood up on the seat of the
motorcycle.

156
00:13:25.364 --> 00:13:29.684
Speaker 1: [gun firing] Balancing, he drew the
messenger and shot one of the drones cleanly out

157
00:13:29.724 --> 00:13:33.704
Speaker 1: of the air. [gun firing] The other
one began shooting at Miranda. Overclock.

158
00:13:33.724 --> 00:13:39.104
Speaker 1: [machine clicking] Time slowed,
creating a shocking feeling of vertigo.

159
00:13:39.704 --> 00:13:44.644
Speaker 1: Ethan ignored the human weakness and
let his accelerometers do the balancing. He

160
00:13:44.704 --> 00:13:49.624
Speaker 1: watched a bullet sink into Miranda's
body in gruesome slow motion.

161
00:13:50.444 --> 00:13:55.044
Speaker 1: Ethan's second mind flagged a new
threat on his HUD with a yellow warning symbol.

162
00:13:55.824 --> 00:14:01.724
Speaker 1: Oh, what now? A cockroach the size of
a dog sailed in slow

163
00:14:01.864 --> 00:14:07.644
Speaker 1: motion through the air. The human
head on its back watched Ethan

164
00:14:07.744 --> 00:14:12.704
Speaker 1: serenely as it flew, its mouth open
in a little O shape.

165
00:14:13.544 --> 00:14:19.004
Speaker 1: Disturbing as it was, it wasn't on a
collision path with him. Release

166
00:14:19.084 --> 00:14:24.504
Speaker 1: overclock. [machine clicking] The
corpse nest collided with the drone, taking it
out

167
00:14:24.544 --> 00:14:28.624
Speaker 1: of the air and shattering its frame
against the wall. Then the creature, still

168
00:14:28.664 --> 00:14:33.204
Speaker 1: living, because apparently even
demons realized that cockroaches were
unkillable,

169
00:14:34.384 --> 00:14:39.624
Speaker 1: leapt toward the cloud of explosive
drones. The simple machines covered it, then

170
00:14:39.804 --> 00:14:44.804
Speaker 1: detonated, [explosion] taking out a
large number of their own in the process.

171
00:14:44.904 --> 00:14:50.724
Speaker 1: [motorcycles revving] Miranda's
motorcycle swerved, then slowed. She fell from
the

172
00:14:50.784 --> 00:14:54.424
Speaker 1: bike at a still lethal speed, rolling
and scraping against the ground.

173
00:14:54.584 --> 00:14:59.124
Speaker 1: [tires screeching] Without even
thinking, Ethan dismounted and ran to her. A
wide

174
00:14:59.204 --> 00:15:04.144
Speaker 1: smear of blood ran from her mouth
down her neck. She looked up at him with one

175
00:15:04.184 --> 00:15:04.984
Speaker 1: annoyed eye.

176
00:15:06.524 --> 00:15:07.024
Speaker 3: Leave me.

177
00:15:08.224 --> 00:15:13.084
Speaker 1: No. Ethan got an arm under her and
dragged her through a blown-out door into a

178
00:15:13.144 --> 00:15:18.204
Speaker 1: building, moving in the direction the
corpse nest had come from. He waited just

179
00:15:18.264 --> 00:15:22.844
Speaker 1: inside the doorway. A gunner drone
zipped in to follow them. Ethan snatched it out

180
00:15:22.864 --> 00:15:27.464
Speaker 1: of the air and smashed it against the
wall. [drone crashing] He pulled the gun from

181
00:15:27.524 --> 00:15:32.004
Speaker 1: the broken device and handed it to
Miranda, pointing at the simple firing
mechanism.

182
00:15:32.924 --> 00:15:38.704
Speaker 1: Here. She crawled toward the wall and
leaned against it. Blood pattered the ground

183
00:15:38.764 --> 00:15:39.484
Speaker 1: beneath her.

184
00:15:40.844 --> 00:15:41.804
Speaker 3: I still hate you.

185
00:15:43.464 --> 00:15:47.264
Speaker 1: Get in line. Miranda snorted a
humorless laugh.

186
00:15:47.844 --> 00:15:48.404
Speaker 3: The others?

187
00:15:49.084 --> 00:15:54.464
Speaker 1: A series of explosions outside
answered her question in the worst possible way.

188
00:15:54.604 --> 00:15:58.124
Speaker 1: [explosions] The sound of motorcycles
died abruptly.

189
00:15:59.604 --> 00:16:04.884
Speaker 3: Go. Take those bastards down at the
source. My mom was New Hope.

190
00:16:06.064 --> 00:16:11.624
Speaker 3: She killed my dad to get me and my
brother out. That place broke her, holy man.

191
00:16:12.264 --> 00:16:17.684
Speaker 1: She met his eyes with her own. An old
rage simmered there.

192
00:16:18.704 --> 00:16:20.664
Speaker 3: It needs breaking.

193
00:16:21.624 --> 00:16:27.444
Speaker 1: Ethan nodded once. No heroics this
time. You gonna be all right?

194
00:16:29.044 --> 00:16:31.944
Speaker 3: I'll live. There's enough juice in me
to heal.

195
00:16:32.583 --> 00:16:37.744
Speaker 1: Ethan searched for a way to the
rooftop, and his eyes found the stairwell door.
But

196
00:16:37.804 --> 00:16:43.644
Speaker 1: he paused before leaving. I'm, uh,
sorry about Eddie.

197
00:16:44.404 --> 00:16:47.004
Speaker 1: There was a sharp intake of breath
behind him.

198
00:16:48.244 --> 00:16:51.264
Speaker 3: Yeah, well, he was an asshole.

199
00:16:52.464 --> 00:16:52.824
